      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "I was re-reading the entire thread (as one does (to decided if I know enough to offer to design the 76 0.5x0.5 CoB PCB that has yet to exist)) and I am actually a little concerned about the vias in the encapsulation region. \nAre we really sure this is okay ? \n> Open vias should not be used in the encapsulation area of the COB design due to\n> capillary wicking and leakage.\nsource: [PCB design guidelines for chip on board (COB) applications](https://www.pi.infn.it/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/low_cost_cob_guidelines.pdf) - part of the original doc linked at the very start of the channel",
